"""Generate all numerical physical diagnostic claims from recorded artifacts."""
import argparse,json,pathlib
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
parser=argparse.ArgumentParser();parser.add_argument('--check',action='store_true');args=parser.parse_args()
p=json.loads((ROOT/'reports/physics/flight-comparison.json').read_text())
v=json.loads((ROOT/'reports/physics/independent-verifier.json').read_text())
lines=['# Public flight diagnostic','','**Negative accuracy finding:** the longer-horizon errors do not support a flight-accuracy claim. Physical validation remains false. No parameter was fitted or changed after these results.','','## Scope','','This compares the production rigid-body `rk4Step` and timestep quaternion normalization with logged Brushless flights. It bypasses the full PhysicsEngine actuator, aerodynamic, battery, contact, sensor and controller pipeline. It uses the dataset authors\' force conversion and loaded-aircraft mass/inertia, rather than the brushed Q-learning reference configuration. These are externally supplied inputs, not independently validated physical parameters.','','The public dataset is [IDSIA nanodrone-sysid-benchmark](https://github.com/idsia-robotics/nanodrone-sysid-benchmark), pinned at `'+p['provenance']['datasetCommit']+'`. The original repository lacked time-aligned flight logs; this diagnostic uses newly located external data. The upstream authors label the three Melon flights as test data. No fitting uses them here.','','## All flights','','| Input file | Rows | Windows per horizon | Horizon (s) | Position RMSE (m) | Velocity RMSE (m/s) | Attitude RMSE (rad) | Body-rate RMSE (rad/s) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for flight in p['flights']:
 for m in flight['metrics']:lines.append('| '+flight['filename']+f" | {flight['rows']} | {m['windows']} | {m['horizonSteps']*.01:.2f} | "+' | '.join(f'{x:.6f}' for x in m['rmse'])+' |')
lines+=['','## Descriptive intervals across independent flight units','','| Horizon (s) | Metric | Mean per-flight RMSE | 95% flight-bootstrap CI | Independent flights |','|---|---|---:|---|---:|']
for s in p['summary']:
 for m in s['metrics']:lines.append(f"| {s['horizonSteps']*.01:.2f} | {m['metric']} | {m['estimate']:.6f} | [{m['ci95'][0]:.6f}, {m['ci95'][1]:.6f}] | {s['independentFlightUnits']} |")
lines+=['','Each flight is an independent unit; overlapping clock history and within-flight windows are not independent flights. Only three flights limit bootstrap coverage. The source clock spacing and horizons were frozen before prediction. The one-step position error is dominated by a short propagation interval and does not establish long-horizon physical accuracy. No statistical-significance or controller-robustness claim is made.','','Long-horizon disagreement may reflect model/parameter mismatch and unmodeled dynamics; this diagnostic does not identify their individual contributions. No measured data were used to improve the simulator. Motor lag, BET and command-to-thrust, production mixer, drag/gust response, battery cutoff/endurance, sensor timing/noise, contact, full flight control and the brushed residual policy remain unvalidated.','','## Reproduction and verification','','The [preregistration](preregistration.md) and scripts were committed before execution. [flight-comparison.json](flight-comparison.json) contains raw predicted/reference states, all input hashes and execution-source hashes; [independent-verifier.json](independent-verifier.json) recomputes their metrics without production imports; [determinism.json](determinism.json) records double clean-worktree replay.','','```bash','git clone https://github.com/idsia-robotics/nanodrone-sysid-benchmark.git /tmp/copter-flight-data','git -C /tmp/copter-flight-data checkout '+p['provenance']['datasetCommit'],'git worktree add --detach /tmp/copter-physics-source '+p['provenance']['sourceCommit'],'cd /tmp/copter-physics-source','npm ci','node --import tsx scripts/physics/compare-flight.ts /tmp/copter-flight-data','python scripts/physics/verify-flight.py','```','','For double replay from the registered execution source use `python scripts/physics/replay-compare.py /tmp/copter-flight-data`. The upstream dataset is fetched rather than vendored; its source does not provide an explicit dataset redistribution license. Availability of a public repository does not imply a redistribution grant.','','Independent verification: '+str(v['passed'])+' passing checks, '+str(v['failed'])+' failures. Numerical checks certify recorded-data consistency, not physical-model adequacy.']
value='\n'.join(lines)+'\n';path=ROOT/'reports/physics/comparison.md'
if args.check:
 if path.read_text()!=value:raise SystemExit('Physical diagnostic claim drift')
 print('Physical diagnostic claims checked.')
else:path.write_text(value)
